---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SectionLabel from "../components/SectionLabel.astro";

const topics = [
	"Growing into staff engineering",
	"Technical leadership, with or without management",
	"Architecture and systems thinking",
	"Careers, and the occasional hard decision",
];

// Flip to "full" when at capacity — mirrors the design's availability prop.
const availability: "open" | "full" = "open";

const col = "mx-auto max-w-[700px] px-5";
const prose = "text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-pretty text-ink-soft";
---

<Layout title="Mentoring — Lawrence Job" crumbs={[{ label: "Mentoring" }]}>
	<header class:list={[col, "pt-[clamp(56px,8vw,110px)]"]}>
		<h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(38px,5vw,60px)] leading-[1.04] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">
			Mentoring
		</h1>
		<p class="mt-6.5 text-[clamp(16.5px,1.6vw,19px)] leading-[1.7] text-pretty text-ink-soft">
			I’ve been mentoring engineers for years — sometimes formally, mostly not. I keep doing it because I had good
			mentors, and it made all the difference.
		</p>
	</header>

	<section class:list={[col, "pt-[clamp(40px,6vw,64px)]"]}>
		<SectionLabel class="mb-4.5">Who it’s for</SectionLabel>
		<p class={prose}>
			Two kinds of people tend to get the most out of this: people who are <span class="text-ink"
				>new to product or engineering</span
			> and finding their feet, and experienced engineers working out <span class="text-ink"
				>the next step — to senior and beyond</span
			>. Both are welcome, and you don’t need to arrive with the right questions. Working out what to ask is part of
			it.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class:list={[col, "pt-[clamp(40px,6vw,64px)]"]}>
		<SectionLabel class="mb-4.5">What it looks like</SectionLabel>
		<p class={prose}>
			Usually a conversation every few weeks. Sometimes there’s a specific problem to work through; sometimes it’s
			just taking stock. The agenda is yours — I’m there to ask questions, share what I’ve seen, and occasionally
			disagree with you.
		</p>
		<ul class="mt-7 border-t border-hairline">
			{
				topics.map((topic) => (
					<li class="flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-hairline py-4 text-base text-ink-soft">
						<span class="flex-none text-[13px] text-copper" aria-hidden="true">
							·
						</span>
						{topic}
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class:list={[col, "pt-[clamp(40px,6vw,64px)]"]}>
		<SectionLabel class="mb-4.5">One or two at a time</SectionLabel>
		<p class={prose}>
			I keep it to one or two mentees at a time, so I can do it properly. If there’s no room when you ask, I’ll say so
			honestly — and it’s never a bother to be asked.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class:list={[col, "pt-[clamp(40px,6vw,64px)] pb-[clamp(56px,8vw,96px)]"]}>
		<SectionLabel class="mb-4.5">Getting in touch</SectionLabel>
		<p class:list={[prose, "mb-5"]}>
			The easiest way to reach me is LinkedIn. Tell me a little about where you are and what you’re working towards —
			no need for anything formal.
		</p>

		<div class="mb-5 flex items-center gap-2.5 text-sm text-ink-mute">
			{
				availability === "open" ? (
					<>
						<span class="h-[7px] w-[7px] flex-none bg-copper" aria-hidden="true" />
						<span>Right now: I have space for one more.</span>
					</>
				) : (
					<>
						<span class="h-[7px] w-[7px] flex-none bg-ink-mute" aria-hidden="true" />
						<span>Right now: I’m at capacity — but reach out anyway, and I’ll let you know when a spot opens.</span>
					</>
				)
			}
		</div>

		<a
			href="https://linkedin.com/lawrencejob"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener"
			class="tile flex items-center justify-between gap-6 px-[clamp(20px,3vw,36px)] py-7"
		>
			<span class="font-display text-[clamp(19px,2vw,23px)] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
				Say hello on LinkedIn
			</span>
			<span class="text-xl text-ink-soft" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
		</a>
	</section>
</Layout>
